  "newChecks": [
    "actual catalogue contains 72 ordered entries and every implemented domain",
    "enabling is opt-in, immutable and starts with zero mastery",
    "malformed catalogue entries are rejected",
    "catalogue and returned reports have no mutable aliases into the world",
    "an existing school cannot be reset by re-enabling",
    "one action per tick applies across different gates",
    "untrained casting is rejected without cost or mutation",
    "a qualified practice costs exactly the documented energy and fatigue",
    "low quality practice consumes a turn but earns no qualification",
    "exhaustion and invalid gate ids fail transactionally",
    "three natural qualified practices unlock stage one",
    "natural practice advances by three qualifications and caps at four",
    "automatic training replaces the legacy blessing and charges only once",
    "turning off automatic training preserves ordinary cultural activity",
    "casting quality failure spends the turn and cost but changes no effect fields",
    "all 72 actual gates train and cast in one valid continuous world",
    "all domain paths produce an observed or changed result when available",
    "school history is bounded and owner-qualified",
    "every domain realizes a bounded effect when its target is not saturated",
    "resource effects record actual capacity-limited changes",
    "fully saturated effects report no effect and still cost energy",
    "resource transformation conserves the local sum and obeys capacity",
    "passage keeps owner and history while moving only to an existing town",
    "revelation records current simulated resources with its original timestamp",
    "remembrance only recalls an existing own decision",
    "remembrance rejects foreign and malformed memories before relabeling or effects",
    "standalone gate APIs reject malformed desire associations",
    "snapshot continuation reproduces exact outcomes",
    "body transfer preserves school mastery and memory",
    "host reports include school scope while the core export remains version one",
    "pre-school snapshots continue without an implicit opt-in",
    "foreign owners, actors and events are rejected at both API layers",
    "malformed mastery, chronology, counters and history are rejected"
